  <meta name="context-path" content="<c:out value='${pageContext.request.contextPath}'/>" />
  <title><c:out value="${initParam.appName}" default="LabSync"/> — A calmer way to run your lab</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="css/styles.css" />
</head>
<body>
  <div id="landing" class="landing-page">
    <header class="site-nav shell">
      <a href="#top" class="brand" aria-label="LabSync home"><span class="brand-mark"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span>labsync<span class="brand-period">.</span></span></a>
      <nav class="main-nav" aria-label="Main navigation">
        <a href="#how-it-works">How it works</a><a href="#features">The details</a><a href="#faq">FAQs</a>
      </nav>
      <div class="nav-actions"><button class="nav-login" data-action="login">Sign in</button><button class="button button-light button-small" data-action="demo-student">Open workspace <span>↗</span></button></div>
    </header>

    <main id="top">
      <section class="hero dark-panel">
        <div class="hero-orb orb-one"></div><div class="hero-orb orb-two"></div><div class="hero-grid"></div>
        <div class="hero-content shell">
          <div class="eyebrow eyebrow-light"><span class="pulse-dot"></span> LAB OPERATIONS, REIMAGINED</div>
          <h1>Your lab.<br><em>Without the chaos.</em></h1>
          <p class="hero-copy">One considered space to book equipment, report issues, and keep every practical session moving.</p>
          <div class="hero-buttons"><button class="button button-light" data-action="demo-student">Explore the workspace <span class="button-arrow">↗</span></button><a class="text-link text-link-light" href="#how-it-works">See how it works <span>↓</span></a></div>
          <div class="hero-footnote"><span class="avatar-stack"><b>AS</b><b>MJ</b><b>RK</b></span><span>Made for the people who make things work.</span><span class="footnote-divider">·</span><span>JECRC · Lab concept</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-float float-left"><span class="float-icon">↗</span><div><strong>Booking confirmed</strong><small>Raspberry Pi 5 Kit · 10:00 AM</small></div><span class="mini-check">✓</span></div>
        <div class="hero-float float-right"><span class="float-label">LIVE STATUS</span><strong>06 <small>/ 08</small></strong><span class="float-caption">Resources ready to use</span><div class="mini-bars"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div></div>
        <div class="hero-bottom-rule shell"><span>LESS ADMIN. MORE MAKING.</span><span>SCROLL TO EXPLORE&nbsp; ↓</span><span>01 — 04</span></div>
      </section>

      <section id="how-it-works" class="section section-paper intro-section">
        <div class="shell intro-grid"><div><div class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-number">01</span> A BETTER LAB DAY</div><h2>Less chasing.<br><em>More doing.</em></h2></div><div class="intro-copy"><p>Shared lab resources are valuable. Managing them shouldn't feel like another experiment.</p><p>LabSync keeps the small-but-important details in one place: what is free, who has booked it, and what needs fixing before the next session.</p><button class="quiet-link" data-action="demo-student">Take a look around <span>↗</span></button></div></div>
        <div class="shell workflow-cards">
          <article class="workflow-card"><div class="card-topline"><span>01 / FIND</span><span class="tiny-icon">⌕</span></div><div class="workflow-icon icon-search">⌕</div><h3>Know what's ready.</h3><p>Browse equipment by lab, category, and live status before you walk across campus.</p><div class="mini-resource-row"><span class="resource-chip-dot"></span><span>GPU Workstation 03</span><b>Available</b></div></article>
          <article class="workflow-card"><div class="card-topline"><span>02 / RESERVE</span><span class="tiny-icon">↗</span></div><div class="workflow-icon icon-calendar">▦</div><h3>Make the time yours.</h3><p>Choose a time slot. LabSync checks for clashes before it confirms your booking.</p><div class="mini-calendar"><span>MON</span><b>14</b><small>10:00 — 11:00</small><i>Confirmed</i></div></article>
          <article class="workflow-card workflow-card-dark"><div class="card-topline"><span>03 / MAINTAIN</span><span class="tiny-icon">＋</span></div><div class="workflow-icon icon-wrench">⌁</div><h3>Catch issues early.</h3><p>Report a fault in context. An unresolved issue flags that resource for maintenance.</p><div class="maintenance-pill"><span></span> Network Analyzer NA-02 <b>In repair</b></div></article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="features" class="section section-teal feature-section">
        <div class="shell feature-intro"><div><div class="eyebrow eyebrow-light"><span class="eyebrow-number">02</span> THE WHOLE PICTURE</div><h2>Small details.<br><em>Fewer surprises.</em></h2></div><p>From your first booking to the final maintenance check, every detail has a place.</p></div>
        <div class="shell feature-showcase">
          <div class="showcase-visual"><div class="showcase-window"><div class="showcase-window-bar"><span class="window-dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span>LABSYNC / OVERVIEW</span><span class="window-live"><i></i> LIVE</span></div><div class="showcase-body"><div class="showcase-greeting"><small>MONDAY, OCTOBER 28</small><strong>A smoother day starts here.</strong><span>All your lab essentials, in one view.</span></div><div class="showcase-metrics"><div><small>Resources ready</small><strong>06 <b>↗</b></strong><span>of 08 total</span></div><div><small>Active bookings</small><strong>12</strong><span>across 4 labs</span></div><div><small>Open issues</small><strong>02 <b class="orange-b">!</b></strong><span>1 high priority</span></div></div><div class="showcase-lower"><div class="showcase-table"><div class="table-title">Resource pulse <span>View all ↗</span></div><div class="fake-row"><span class="fake-square">Pi</span><span><b>Raspberry Pi 5 Kit</b><small>IoT Studio</small></span><em class="state-ready">Available</em></div><div class="fake-row"><span class="fake-square fake-square-coral">NA</span><span><b>Network Analyzer NA-02</b><small>Network Lab</small></span><em class="state-repair">Maintenance</em></div><div class="fake-row"><span class="fake-square fake-square-mint">GPU</span><span><b>GPU Workstation 03</b><small>AI Lab</small></span><em class="state-ready">Available</em></div></div><div class="showcase-next"><small>NEXT BOOKING</small><div class="date-tile"><b>29</b><span>OCT</span></div><strong>Arduino Mega Kit</strong><small>10:00 AM — 11:30 AM</small><div class="confirm-line"><span>Confirmed</span><i>✓</i></div></div></div></div></div><div class="showcase-annotation annotation-left"><span>01</span> Clear at a glance</div><div class="showcase-annotation annotation-right"><span>02</span> Nothing slips through</div></div>
          <div class="feature-list"><article><span>01</span><div><h3>One source of truth</h3><p>Resources, bookings, and faults stay connected instead of scattered across messages and registers.</p></div><b>↗</b></article><article><span>02</span><div><h3>Conflict-aware booking</h3><p>Overlapping time slots are blocked before they become a problem.</p></div><b>↗</b></article><article><span>03</span><div><h3>Maintenance that matters</h3><p>Unresolved issues make equipment unavailable until the issue is resolved.</p></div><b>↗</b></article><button class="button button-outline-light" data-action="demo-student">Try the interactive demo <span>↗</span></button></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section section-paper principle-section"><div class="shell principle-grid"><div><div class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-number">03</span> BUILT AROUND REAL WORK</div><h2>Less software<br><em>to fight with.</em></h2><p class="principle-copy">LabSync is intentionally practical. Students see what they need; administrators see what needs attention.</p></div><div class="principle-stack"><div class="principle-card"><span class="principle-icon">◌</span><div><h3>Students stay self-sufficient</h3><p>Find resources, reserve a time, and keep track of your requests without asking around.</p></div><span class="principle-number">01</span></div><div class="principle-card"><span class="principle-icon">⌘</span><div><h3>Admins see the whole system</h3><p>Manage inventory and bookings, triage reports, and close the loop on repairs.</p></div><span class="principle-number">02</span></div><div class="principle-card"><span class="principle-icon">↗</span><div><h3>Every change leaves a record</h3><p>Booking and issue states make it easier to understand what happened.</p></div><span class="principle-number">03</span></div></div></div></section>

      <section id="faq" class="section section-paper faq-section"><div class="shell faq-grid"><div><div class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-number">04</span> A FEW GOOD QUESTIONS</div><h2>Before you<br><em>jump in.</em></h2><p>Want to see the actual workflow? Open the workspace and try both roles.</p><button class="quiet-link" data-action="demo-student">Open LabSync <span>↗</span></button></div><div class="faq-list"><details open><summary>Who is LabSync for?<span>＋</span></summary><p>It is a concept application for college labs where students share equipment and lab administrators handle inventory and maintenance.</p></details><details><summary>Can I book a resource with an open issue?<span>＋</span></summary><p>No. A resource with an unresolved issue is marked for maintenance and cannot be booked until the issue is resolved.</p></details><details><summary>Does the demo save my changes?<span>＋</span></summary><p>Yes. The browser demo saves changes in local storage on this device. When deployed to Tomcat, the Java backend stores records in the configured JDBC database.</p></details><details><summary>Which technologies power the project?<span>＋</span></summary><p>Java Servlets, JDBC, H2 by default (MySQL can be configured), JSP/JSTL, HTML, CSS, JavaScript and Apache Tomcat 9.</p></details></div></div></section>
      <section class="end-cta dark-panel"><div class="hero-orb orb-one"></div><div class="shell end-cta-inner"><div class="eyebrow eyebrow-light">READY WHEN YOU ARE</div><h2>Before the next lab,<br><em>make it run smoother.</em></h2><button class="button button-light" data-action="demo-student">Open the workspace <span>↗</span></button></div><footer class="site-footer shell"><a href="#top" class="brand brand-footer"><span class="brand-mark"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span>labsync<span class="brand-period">.</span></span></a><span>A college lab, thoughtfully connected.</span><span>ADVANCED JAVA LAB PROJECT · 2026—27</span></footer></section>
    </main>
  </div>

  <div id="workspace" class="workspace" hidden>
    <aside class="sidebar"><a href="#" data-action="home" class="brand sidebar-brand"><span class="brand-mark"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span>labsync<span class="brand-period">.</span></span></a><div class="workspace-tag">LAB OPERATIONS</div><div class="sidebar-label">WORKSPACE</div><nav id="sidebarNav" class="sidebar-nav"><button class="side-link active" data-view="overview"><span>◫</span>Overview</button><button class="side-link" data-view="resources"><span>▦</span>Resources</button><button class="side-link" data-view="bookings"><span>◷</span>My bookings</button><button class="side-link" data-view="issues"><span>⌁</span>Issues & repairs</button></nav><div class="sidebar-bottom"><div class="sidebar-help"><span class="help-orb">✳</span><div><strong>Need a hand?</strong><small>Report a resource issue</small></div><button data-action="report-issue" aria-label="Report an issue">↗</button></div><div class="sidebar-user"><div class="user-avatar" id="userAvatar">AS</div><div class="user-details"><strong id="sidebarUserName">Aarav Sharma</strong><small id="sidebarUserRole">Student</small></div><button data-action="logout" class="logout-button" title="Sign out">↪</button></div></div></aside>
    <main class="app-main"><header class="app-topbar"><div class="breadcrumbs"><span>LabSync</span><b>/</b><strong id="currentCrumb">Overview</strong></div><div class="topbar-actions"><span class="server-pill"><i></i><span id="connectionLabel">Demo workspace</span></span><button class="icon-button" data-action="quick-book" title="Book a resource">＋</button><button class="topbar-avatar" id="topbarAvatar" data-action="profile">AS</button></div></header><div class="app-content"><div id="view" aria-live="polite"></div><footer class="app-footer"><span>LABSYNC / LAB OPERATIONS</span><span>Make room for good work. <b>↗</b></span></footer></div></main>
  </div>

  <div class="modal-backdrop" id="authModal" hidden><div class="modal modal-auth" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="authTitle"><button class="modal-close" data-action="close-auth" aria-label="Close">×</button><div class="modal-kicker">WELCOME BACK</div><h2 id="authTitle">Step back<br><em>into the lab.</em></h2><p class="modal-description">Sign in to manage bookings and equipment.</p><form id="loginForm" class="form-stack"><label>Email address<input id="loginEmail" name="email" type="email" autocomplete="username" placeholder="you@college.edu" required /></label><label>Password<input id="loginPassword" name="password" type="password" autocomplete="current-password" placeholder="Enter your password" required /></label><div id="loginError" class="form-error" hidden></div><button type="submit" class="button button-dark button-full">Sign in <span>↗</span></button></form><div class="demo-divider"><span>OR TRY A DEMO ROLE</span></div><div class="demo-roles"><button data-action="demo-student"><span class="role-icon">S</span><span><b>Student demo</b><small>Book resources & report faults</small></span><span>↗</span></button><button data-action="demo-admin"><span class="role-icon role-icon-admin">A</span><span><b>Admin demo</b><small>Manage inventory & repairs</small></span><span>↗</span></button></div><div class="demo-credentials">Demo login: <b>student@labsync.local / student123</b><br />Admin: <b>admin@labsync.local / admin123</b></div></div></div>
  <div class="modal-backdrop" id="actionModal" hidden><div class="modal modal-action" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="actionModalTitle"><button class="modal-close" data-action="close-action" aria-label="Close">×</button><div id="actionModalContent"></div></div></div>
  <div id="toastRegion" class="toast-region" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"></div>
  <script src="js/app.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
